# Canvas Grid & Overlay Contracts

These invariants were established after repeated regressions (v8 → v12). They are non-negotiable.

## Grid Contract

- The canvas grid MUST be dynamic: `backgroundSize` and `backgroundPosition` on `.workflow-canvas` must be derived from `zoom` and `pan` state via inline styles.
- `GRID_SIZE` from `constants.ts` is the single source of truth for grid spacing.
- The CSS `background-image` defines the gradient pattern; JS inline styles control size and position.
- When `gridEnabled` is false, the `no-grid` class hides the background — this is the only toggle mechanism.

## ExecutionOverlay Positioning Contract

- The overlay uses `position: fixed` with JS-computed `top` from a `ResizeObserver` on `.workflow-canvas`.
- Horizontal position is CSS-owned (`right: 16px` for helm, `right: 24px` for standard).
- Vertical position is JS-owned (`top` style prop from canvas observation).
- Drag uses an additive `transform: translate(offsetX, offsetY)` on top of the CSS/JS base position.
- `dragOffset` MUST reset to `{x:0, y:0}` when the overlay reopens (new deployment or "View Logs").
- Only the title bar div is the drag handle — log content area stops propagation for text selection.

## What You Must NOT Do

- Do not add `top`, `left`, or `right` inline styles that compete with the CSS anchor.
- Do not replace the `ResizeObserver`-based `canvasTop` with a one-shot `getBoundingClientRect` call.
- Do not make the entire overlay a drag handle — only the title bar.
- Do not use `!important` on positioning properties without a comment explaining the conflict.
- Do not change `backgroundSize`/`backgroundPosition` to static CSS values.
